@crew vance
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== greet
? endgame:early
- {hi}, {nick}. The transfer note is off your file. It was a short note.   #funny

== chat
? endgame:early
- The regulation on staying aboard is one line long. I've read it four times.   #funny
? endgame
- Three things. Breakfast on time. Rest on rest days. And you're seventh on the list now.   #funny
- New column on the treadmill board: days aboard. You're climbing it without trying.   #funny
? endgame:early
- Your staying is noted, approved and filed. With some satisfaction.   #warm
? endgame:early
- Gull wrote a poem about the crossing back. I'm told it rhymed "Line" with "fine". Twice.   #funny
? endgame tier>=friend
- I'll say it once. The ship is better with you on her. As you were.   #warm
? endgame beat:vance.5 tier>=close
- Gull has written you a poem. Gull would like you never to read it. Gull is firm on this.   #funny

== feel
? endgame
- I left the bridge on time three days running. The Counsellor is delighted. I'm adjusting.

== bye
? endgame
- Carry on. At an ordinary pace. That is an order, of a kind.
